"""Writes the ImageGen prompt files for the Gloam Circuit arena art (inputs of scripts/gen-image.py). Run from this folder."""
STYLE = ("Style: 2D top-down action game environment art for KYNTRAZE: FRACTURE RUSH, crisp cel-shaded pixel-art look (clean dark navy-black outline about 3-4 px, flat 2-3 step shading, hard stepped edges, NO blur, NO painterly noise, NO text, NO letters). "
 "Palette: dark navy steel (#1b2735, #2a3a4d, #0c1522), cold teal circuit inlay (#3fa8b2) used sparingly as thin glowing lines, tiny amber (#e3a766) marker lights ONLY as small accents. Everything must be LOW-CONTRAST and dark-to-mid values (it sits on a dark floor behind a hero), no bright whites, no red, no orange fills. "
 "The first reference image shows the existing floor tiles (match their navy steel plating, rivets and lightning-glint texture). The second shows the hero Kai for scale: props must feel sized against him. ")
RAISED = "View: steeply raised top-down three-quarter (about 60 degrees from horizontal): show the big top face and only a SHORT front face (low relief), never a tall side elevation. "
FLAT = "View: straight top-down; these lie flat on the floor. "
W = lambda n, s: open(n + "-prompt.txt", "w").write(s)

W("props", "Sprite sheet of 6 SOLID machine-floor props for the arena 'The Gloam Circuit' (an industrial powered machine hall). " + STYLE + RAISED +
 "Draw EXACTLY 6 props on flat magenta (#ff00ff), 3 columns x 2 rows, far apart, nothing cropped, each fully inside its own cell, each ground-anchored with a flat base, NO cast shadow, no floor under them. Proportions are footprint width : depth (the ground area they cover), keep these ratios exactly:\n"
 "1. GENERATOR: a squat humming generator unit, footprint ratio 125:55 (wide, shallow), ribbed housing, one teal glowing core slot, two small amber lights.\n"
 "2. FREIGHT POD: a long armored cargo pod lying vertically, footprint ratio 90:180 (narrow and long, taller than wide), segmented hull plates, a teal seam, dull dark amber-grey hazard-chevron end cap.\n"
 "3. CONSOLE BANK: a low long control console bank, footprint ratio 155:64, dark screens showing faint teal waveforms, rows of tiny buttons, cable stubs.\n"
 "4. REACTOR BLOCK: a heavy low reactor containment block, footprint ratio 165:70, thick plated lid, a circular teal-glow vent on top, coolant pipes on the sides.\n"
 "5. VENT STACK: a long low ventilation stack unit, footprint ratio 145:48, row of vent slats, dark grille, pipe stubs.\n"
 "6. CRATE STACK: a neat stack of three armored supply crates, footprint ratio 120:80, riveted lids, dull stencil-like marker bars (no letters), one teal strap.\n")
W("decor", "Sprite sheet of 9 floor DECALS and flat floor props for the arena 'The Gloam Circuit' (industrial powered machine hall). " + STYLE + FLAT +
 "Draw EXACTLY 9 items on flat magenta (#ff00ff), 3 columns x 3 rows, far apart, nothing cropped, each fully inside its own cell, NO cast shadows, dark and low-contrast:\n"
 "1. CABLE BUNDLE A: a thick bundle of dark cables lying in a gentle S curve, about 200 x 40 proportion, with two clamp rings.\n2. CABLE BUNDLE B: a different cable run with a loop and a small junction box, about 180 x 50 proportion.\n"
 "3. FLOOR GRATE: a square steel maintenance grate with dark slots and bolts, about 96 x 96, seen from above.\n4. SCORCH A: a burnt black scorch mark on steel plating with faint cracked edges, irregular blob about 130 px.\n5. SCORCH B: another scorch / blast mark, more radial with tiny debris chips, about 130 px.\n"
 "6. CRACK A: a long jagged crack running through the metal plating with a faint teal glow deep inside, about 170 x 60.\n7. CRACK B: a shorter branching crack, no glow, about 150 x 90.\n"
 "8. HAZARD STRIPES: a flat painted warning strip of diagonal dull amber-grey and black stripes, scuffed and worn, about 192 x 48 (muted, dark, not bright).\n9. COOLANT PUDDLE: a dark shallow puddle of coolant fluid with a faint teal sheen and a couple of drips, organic outline, about 120 x 70.\n")
W("glyph", "A single large circular floor emblem for the arena 'The Gloam Circuit' (industrial powered machine hall). " + STYLE + "View: straight top-down; it is inlaid flat in the floor. " +
 "Draw ONE perfectly circular concentric inlay glyph centred in the image on flat magenta (#ff00ff): an outer ring of segmented dark steel plates, a thinner teal-glowing circuit ring with small notches and four cardinal node brackets, an inner ring of chevron marks, and a recessed central core disc with a faint teal glow. Symmetric, restrained, dark, low-contrast (the glow is faint and thin), diameter about 560 px, no text, no letters, a wide margin of magenta all around.\n")
W("rim", "Two environment pieces for the arena 'The Gloam Circuit' (industrial powered machine hall). " + STYLE + "View: from above and slightly in front, looking at the inner face of a perimeter wall that borders the arena floor. " +
 "Draw on flat magenta (#ff00ff), far apart, nothing cropped:\n"
 "A) RIM STRIP (wide image, 2.67:1 proportion, about 256x96): a perfectly HORIZONTALLY TILEABLE section of the arena perimeter wall face: heavy dark steel wall panels with vertical seams every ~64 px, rivets, a recessed cable conduit, a thin glowing teal edge light strip along the BOTTOM edge where the wall meets the floor, a darker top edge. The pattern must repeat seamlessly left to right. Fully opaque rectangle, no magenta inside it.\n"
 "B) CORNER (square, about 128x128): the top-left corner piece of the same wall: the wall face running along the top and the left side meeting in a mitred reinforced corner post with a small dull amber marker light and a teal edge light following both inner edges. Fully opaque square.\n")
W("fx", "Sprite sheet of 4 environment effect textures for the game KYNTRAZE: FRACTURE RUSH. All hostile hazard art in hot crimson (#ff3050 / #ff3a6e) and bone-white (#e8dcc8) ONLY, no orange, no gold, no cyan, crisp hard-edged cel-shaded stripes, no blur, no text. Draw EXACTLY 4 items on flat magenta (#ff00ff), 2 columns x 2 rows, each a wide horizontal strip about 3:1 filling most of its cell, far apart, nothing cropped:\n"
 "1. SURGE WARNING STRIP: a horizontal danger-lane texture: bold diagonal hazard stripes alternating translucent dark crimson and bone-white-edged crimson, with a repeating row of chevrons pointing right along the middle, outlined top and bottom by thin crimson lines. Must tile seamlessly left to right.\n"
 "2. SURGE WARNING STRIP VARIANT: same layout but chevrons shifted half a period and stripes a half step offset (animation frame two).\n"
 "3. SURGE ACTIVE STRIP: a horizontal surge of live energy: a white-hot core band with crimson electric arcs and jagged lightning forks along it, hard pixel-art edges, glowing crimson outer band, tileable left to right.\n"
 "4. SURGE ACTIVE STRIP VARIANT: same but arcs and forks in different places (animation frame two).\n")
W("amb", "Sprite sheet of ambience textures for a dark sci-fi machine-hall arena (game KYNTRAZE: FRACTURE RUSH): crisp look, no text. Draw on flat magenta (#ff00ff), far apart, nothing cropped:\n"
 "A) 6 DRIFTING MOTES in a row at the top, each in its own cell: tiny soft round sparks of pale teal-white light, 4-10 px, varied, with a faint 1px glow, like dust catching a cold light.\n"
 "B) 1 large SQUARE FOG TEXTURE at the bottom, big, about 400x400, filling its own region completely edge to edge (no magenta inside it): soft drifting cold haze: layered dark-teal and navy wisps of mist on a pale-grey-to-navy field, low contrast, no hard edges, no objects, it must be a flat full-square soft texture whose edges are about the same tone as its centre.\n")
W("card", "Key-art illustration (widescreen 16:9) for the arena-selection card of THE GLOAM CIRCUIT, an original arena in a premium 2D action-survival game: a vast dark industrial machine hall seen from a raised top-down three-quarter view: dark navy steel plated floor with long glowing teal circuit lanes crossing in the middle, a large circular floor glyph with a faint teal glow at the centre, heavy generators, a reactor block and cargo pods standing around, cable bundles, coolant puddles, a thin teal-lit perimeter wall in the distance, drifting pale motes and cold haze, deep vignette. Cinematic, moody, premium, crisp cel-shaded pixel-art look matching the reference tiles (clean dark outlines, flat shading, hard edges, no blur), low-key lighting with the brightest accent being the teal lanes and a few tiny amber marker lights. NO characters, NO UI, NO text, NO letters, no crimson.\n")
